First, a change of my own that I would like to see:
All items have a "power" (integer) associated with them.  Whenever an item
(or items) is polymorphed, it would only turn into items of the same type
of _smaller_ power.  This would eliminate the sort of endless polypiling, 
I find myself doing, but still maintain some of the utility of disposing of 
things you don't need.  Also, the wand of wishing problem is a natural result 
of WOWs having higher power than other wands.

The type of magic an item produces, its plusses, its number of charges, etc
would all count into its power.  (A calculation that would be easy to make
by computer at game time.)  This might mean that a powerful wand with lots
of charges might be morphable into a WOW with say, one charge.  Which is fine 
with me.

You might then have a wand of limited wishes, with which you could only get
items of a certain power or less.  Ditto for normal WOWs: using a power rating
could naturally rule out getting a blessed +27 artifact, and give you a 
less powerful item instead.

